@section('content')
  <h1>{{ $title }}</h1>
  <p>Actions are the buttons that change records. The panel has page actions, which work on the whole list, and row actions, which work on one record.</p>

  <h2>Page actions</h2>
  <p>The list page has a <code>New</code> button, which opens an empty form. The form has a <code>Create</code> button on a new record, and <code>Save</code> on an existing one, plus a <code>Cancel</code> link back to the list.</p>

  <p>The headings use the record's singular name, such as <code>New Tag</code> on the new page and <code>Edit Tag #3</code> on the edit page.</p>

  <h2>Row actions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Edit</strong> opens the record's edit page at <code>/admin/&lt;slug&gt;/&lt;id&gt;/edit</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Delete</strong> posts to <code>/admin/&lt;slug&gt;/&lt;id&gt;/delete</code>, after a confirmation. The record is then deleted with the resource's <code>delete</code> method.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Deleting a record</h2>
  <p>The Delete button asks the browser to confirm with the message <code>Delete this record? This cannot be undone.</code> Cancelling the dialog keeps the record. The confirmation is written in JavaScript: with JavaScript turned off, the delete goes through without asking.</p>
  <p>The delete form carries the panel's token. A missing or wrong token shows the Page Expired page, and nothing is deleted.</p>
  <p>A delete for an id that matches no row returns 404. On success, the panel returns to the list and shows <code>Record deleted.</code>. See <a href="/docs/notifications">Notifications</a>.</p>

  <h2>Not built yet</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Bulk actions.</strong> There is no way to act on several rows at once.</li>
    <li><strong>Custom actions.</strong> A resource cannot add its own buttons in v1.</li>
  </ul>
@endsection
